---
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import InstallOptions from '../../components/shared/InstallOptions.astro';
import { release } from '../../data/release';
---

<DocumentLayout
  route="guide"
  locale="en"
  title="Install deepK on your Mac"
  description="From installing the app to connecting your AI account and granting permissions. Set it up once, and you can translate right from the sentence you are reading."
>
  <section id="install">
    <h2>1. Install the app</h2>
    <p>
      deepK requires an Apple Silicon Mac with macOS {release.minimumMacOS} or later. There is no
      Intel Mac build yet.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6">
      <InstallOptions guideLink={false} locale="en" />
    </div>
    <p>
      If you downloaded the ZIP, unzip it and move <code>deepK.app</code> to your Applications
      folder. The app is notarized, so you do not need to turn off macOS security settings or remove
      the quarantine attribute.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>2. Sign in to the AI account you will use</h2>
    <p>
      deepK translates through the Codex CLI or Claude Code installed on your Mac. Install the one
      you want to use by following its official guide, and sign in with your subscription on this
      Mac.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Official Codex CLI install guide ↗
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/quickstart"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Official Claude Code quickstart ↗
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      After launching deepK, choose a provider in Settings from the menu bar and check the
      connection. Subscription fees and usage limits follow the provider's terms.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>3. Allow macOS permissions</h2>
    <p>
      The deepK app is currently in Korean. In its settings, open 일반 (General) → 권한
      (Permissions) and click <strong>설정 열기…</strong> (Open Settings…) next to the permission
      you need. System Settings opens to that pane with a small guide window. Drag the deepK icon
      from the guide window into the list and turn on the switch. If deepK is already in the list,
      just turn on the switch.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Input Monitoring:</strong> needed to detect pressing ⌘C twice.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Accessibility:</strong> needed to insert a translation where you were typing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Screen Recording (screen-region translation only):</strong> takes one screenshot of
        the rectangle you select to read text in images or games that cannot be copied. In the
        translation window, choose <strong>화면에서 이미지 가져오기</strong> (Get image from
        screen), then <strong>화면 기록 허용</strong> (Allow Screen Recording). Ordinary text and
        clipboard images do not need this permission.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      macOS calls this permission “Screen Recording,” but deepK does not record video or
      continuously watch your screen. It reads your selected region once, or once again when you
      click
      <strong>다시 읽기</strong> (Read again). OCR runs on your Mac; only recognized text goes to
      your chosen official CLI provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      If pressing ⌘C twice is still not detected after you allow it, click
      <strong>감시 다시 연결</strong> (Reconnect Monitoring) on the same screen, or reopen deepK
      with
      <strong>앱 다시 열기…</strong> (Reopen App…). If you moved over from an earlier development
      build and the switch is on but deepK is still not ready, you may need to re-register the
      permission for the installed deepK.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>4. Select a sentence and press ⌘C twice</h2>
    <p>
      In the app you are reading, select a sentence and press the copy shortcut twice in a row. Read
      the result in the small translation window, then copy it or insert it where you were typing if
      you need to. You can also type text in directly to translate it. Translating on a double copy
      is on by default, and you can turn it off in Settings.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>5. Translate images in the same window</h2>
    <p>
      In apps that copy text and images together, select both and press ⌘C twice to bring them into
      the same translation window. Supported X image URLs are loaded from the original server; small
      decorative icons are skipped. If your browser leaves the image out of the copy, or you are
      reading a game that cannot be copied, choose <strong>화면에서 이미지 가져오기</strong>
      (Get image from screen) and draw a rectangle around the text and image.
    </p>
    <p>
      Compare the original and translation side by side. Regions with complex backgrounds or layouts
      may keep the original when they cannot be replaced safely. Loading original images
      automatically is not supported on every website.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Updating and removing</h2>
    <p>
      If you installed with Homebrew, quit deepK and run the commands below. They update the app
      once a new version is published.
    </p>
    <pre><code>brew update
brew upgrade --cask Geuni620/tap/deepk</code></pre>
    <p>
      To remove the app, use the command below. The CLI you installed separately and its login stay
      as they are.
    </p>
    <pre><code>brew uninstall --cask Geuni620/tap/deepk</code></pre>
    <p>
      If you installed from the ZIP, replace or delete the app in your Applications folder. Starting
      with 0.1.1, the app is named <code>deepK.app</code>. If the older <code>DeepK.app</code> is
      still there, do not run both; delete the old one.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>About the current release</h2>
    <p>
      {release.version} brings text and image translation into one window. The release is signed and
      notarized by Apple. Copy formats and screen permissions vary by app; the full flow has not
      been verified on every website, game, or other Mac.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={release.notesUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Release notes ↗
      </a>{' '}
      ·{' '}
      <a href={`${release.repositoryUrl}/issues`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Report an issue ↗
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocumentLayout>
